      "side": 0,
      "message": "That\u0027s exactly where the bug is from.\ncm-\u003efeatures.all_lossless can be changed between frames. We can create a case that the first frame cm-\u003efeatures.all_lossless \u003d 1. In that case, is_restoration_used is true, and all block size is 4x4 (lossless), then the buffer size if only allocated for 4x4 block.\n\nIn the next frame, if we change frame size, and cm-\u003efeatures.all_lossless \u003d 0, is_restoration_used is false, the buffer allocation will not be triggered, leading to memory issue.\n\nIn the new change, we remove the check for cm-\u003efeatures.all_lossless, so that any time frame size changes, the buffer size is reallocated.",
